# The workspace deliberately has no ignore rule of its own here.
#
# It ships empty, so there was nothing to exclude in the first place — and
# excluding it actively breaks the course. The README asks the reader to commit
# after every checkpoint and to `git diff` their work against the reference
# implementation; with `workspace/*/*` ignored, `git add .` stages nothing and
# says nothing, so that whole working method fails silently.
#
# Their work belongs in their history. workspace/.gitignore already keeps the
# dangerous things out of it — state, tfvars, keys, kubeconfig, vault password.

# Terraform: provider binaries are hundreds of megabytes, and state and
# tfvars carry account identifiers and secrets.
**/.terraform/*
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars
!*.tfvars.example
backend.hcl
crash.log

# Credentials and keys, in every form this project mentions them.
*.pem
*.key
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
kubeconfig
*.kubeconfig
vault-password*
.vault_pass*

# Local noise.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
